    // it and its ring: +-1.5 L) -- where the rays are -- with the plane / normal weights and the
    // filter widened to the spacing (sL); the sharp sum takes them too without an own ray. The
    // gather radius thus grows as 1 / sqrt(rho); the lobe disc below adds its footprint.
