    // roughness), so a pixel can find no ray at its own lattice spacing. Before it keeps its env
    // (no splice), the coarser lattices around it (2 L, 4 L, ... up to 16, the rank's coarsest
    // lattice), filter widened to match -- a weak, sparse reflection takes a little blur instead of
    // a pixel left on the probe. (Still nothing on the same plane: the env stands, as before.)
